# version/date track the project's ONE release tag, `reports-v1.0` ("PUBLISH: technical report
# suite v1.0 … first public release", 2026-07-03). The corpus is otherwise continuously published
# and living-versioned per report, so there is no separate software version scheme to cite; the
# `commit` field is what makes a citation exact. Until 2026-08-08 this file carried NO version at
# all and `date-released: 2026-04-08` — three months BEFORE the suite was first published — so
# anyone citing as instructed cited an unversioned, stale artifact.
